  "control_every": 4,
  "comment": [
    "Four scenes, because one cannot exercise every setting. Sun shafts are",
    "strongest with the sun on the horizon and in rain, so at noon under a",
    "clear sky the setting does nothing by construction and reads as free.",
    "Normal maps, corner shading and surface detail act on near surfaces, so a",
    "camera thirty nodes from anything cannot see them either. Lamp shadows",
    "want a lit village after dark. Each variant names the scene it can act in,",
    "and the control is measured inside every scene it is compared against.",
    "",
    "base sets a texture pack. Without one there are no LabPBR maps for the",
    "mat_* strengths to scale, so those settings would multiply nothing and",
    "read as free for that reason rather than any other. base also turns",
    "show_body off: in fly mode the own body draws as a large flat red quad",
    "across the lower sixth of the frame, which is a rendering fault worth",
    "fixing on its own but not part of the scene being measured.",
    "",
    "GOANNA_STORE points at a warmed block store. This world's far field does",
    "not converge from nothing at the vista: a cold run sat there twenty",
    "minutes taking 400,000 blocks and never settled.",
    "",
    "structures places the village. Run once with --build-scene on a world",
    "that has not had it, then never again, or the villages stack.",
    "",
    "scene.png beside the report is what was measured. The first run of this",
    "harness aimed yaw 0 from the spawn and photographed a tree trunk."
  ],
